""" Information fraction phi(sigmaA, sigma) for LLGI map coefficients.

phi = 1 - <posterior variance of E given (data, Ecalc)>/(1 - sigmaA^2),
averaged over the Wilson distribution of Ecalc, the sigmaA model for the
true E given Ecalc, and the measurement error I_obs ~ N(|E|^2, sigma^2)
(all on the E^2 scale). Equivalently phi = (E[<E>^2] - sigmaA^2)/
(1 - sigmaA^2), with <E> the exact posterior mean along the model phase.
The model bias of <E> is sigmaA*(1 - phi), which the bias-reduced map
coefficient removes (mmtbx.refinement.llgi_maps).

Tabulated by deterministic quadrature (llgi_phi_table_generate.py) on the
grid below, for acentric and centric reflections. phi -> 0 as sigma -> inf
like k*sigmaA^2*(1 - sigmaA^2)/sigma^2 (k = 1 acentric, 4 centric); the
table's last column matches this to <1%, and beyond it phi is extrapolated
as (SIGMA[-1]/sigma)^2. Interpolation is bilinear in log(phi/sigmaA^2)
over sigmaA and asinh(sigma/0.02): median relative error 7e-4, worst ~3%
on the grid's interior (an absolute error below 0.002, which changes the
bias correction (1 - phi)*sigmaA by less than 0.002).
"""

